-- and one double count refutes the hypothesis. So a corpus that cannot state the event cannot state
-- the hypothesis either, and every variance, mean error and correlation computed over it is computed
-- under an assumption the corpus has no way to hold. The ChEMBL uncertainty estimate is honest
-- precisely because its authors removed the double counts by hand first.
double-count-not-distinct : (I : Type 0) → (V : Type 0) → (f : I → Measured V) → DoubleCount I V f → (Distinct I V f → Empty)
double-count-not-distinct I V f c = λ d → snd (snd (snd c)) (d (fst c) (fst (snd c)) (fst (snd (snd c))))
